Source: igos-openssl-fips-provider
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Perle Systems <support@perle.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), openssl
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: igos-openssl-fips-provider
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libssl3 (>= 3.0)
# Debian's OpenSSL 3.5 source also builds openssl-provider-fips, which installs
# an UNVALIDATED 3.5 fips.so at the same ossl-modules/fips.so path. Take over
# that path so only the validated 3.1.2 module can ever be loaded.
Conflicts: openssl-provider-fips
Replaces: openssl-provider-fips
Provides: openssl-provider-fips
Description: OpenSSL FIPS 140-3 validated provider (CMVP #4985)
 Ships the pinned, pre-built OpenSSL 3.1.2 FIPS provider (fips.so) that holds
 NIST CMVP certificate #4985, installed into the OpenSSL provider module
 directory (ossl-modules/).
 .
 The provider is version-decoupled from the base library: this validated 3.1.2
 module loads against the system's OpenSSL 3.5 libcrypto. It is inert until
 activated — igOS switches OpenSSL to this provider on
 "set system option fips" (which runs "openssl fipsinstall" to self-test the
 module and generate /run/ssl/fipsmodule.cnf, then points openssl.cnf at it).
 .
 This package only installs the frozen, validated binary; it does not build or
 alter it. It also ships an identity manifest (provider version + SHA-256 of
 the installed fips.so) that vyos-1x checks before and after activating FIPS
 mode, so a substituted module fails closed. It replaces Debian's unvalidated
 openssl-provider-fips. See docs/igos-fips-140-3-design.md (§7.5, §8.1).
